#: src/difficulty/components/hard-sudoku-page/hard-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "Hard boards carry {clueCount} clues and are guaranteed to need at least one fish or wing pattern beyond every subset."
msgstr "困难盘面有 {clueCount} 个已知数字，保证至少需要一种超出所有数组的鱼形或翼形。"

#: src/printable/components/printable-hard-sudoku-page/printable-hard-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "Hard drops to {clueCount} clues, and this is the first printable booklet on the site where subsets alone will not carry you to the end. Every puzzle in it was tested against a solver that already knows every intersection and every subset, and kept only because that solver stalled. What finishes them is a fish or a wing: the <0>X-Wing</0> and its larger and finned relatives, or one of the bivalue wing patterns."
msgstr "困难降到 {clueCount} 个已知数字，这是本站第一本仅靠数组走不到终点的可打印册子。其中每道题都用一个已掌握所有交叉区块和所有数组的解题器测试过，只因为该解题器卡住才被保留。能解开它们的是鱼形或翼形：<0>X-Wing</0> 及其更大的和带鳍的变体，或者某种双候选翼形。"

#: src/difficulty/components/hard-sudoku-page/hard-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "Hard is capped at the W-Wing — a board that resists every fish and wing is graded Nightmare instead."
msgstr "困难以 W-Wing 为上限：用尽所有鱼形和翼形仍然无法突破的盘面，会被评为噩梦。"

